From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] llama: replace the per-layer recurrent-state gather with a cache view when the slot mapping is identity (+6.6% decode)

Every GDN layer materializes its recurrent state before gated_delta_net
runs: build_rs gathers the 2 MB ssm state (get_rows_float_vec, 4.93us) and
build_conv_state gathers the conv window (k_get_rows_float, 1.65us) - 60
launches and ~197us of pure copy kernel time per decode token, plus the
writeback cpy that already exists. The gather exists for seq-copy
migration and rollback-snapshot restore; during steady single-slot decode
its ids are the identity and the copy moves bytes to a new address so the
kernel can read them.

This patch detects that case side-effect-free at graph build time
(llama_memory_recurrent_context::s_copy_main_is_identity: cells[head+i]
.src0 == head+i and no pending rollback restore) and replaces the gather
with a contiguous ggml_view_2d of the cache rows. Byte-identical values
reach the consumer; both get_rows kernels disappear from the decode trace.

Reuse safety: the fork reuses built graphs across decode steps (~27 builds
serve a 256-token completion), and a view bakes its offset at build time
while get_rows refreshes through the s_copy input tensor. The view is
therefore restricted to the single-slot serving shape (n_seqs == 1,
head == 0, n_rs == 1): the baked offset is row 0 always, so a reused view
graph can never go stale, and this is exactly the ranked configuration
(--parallel 1). Multi-slot, migrated, or rollback states fall back to the
stock gather (verified live: prompt-phase builds with src0 still unset
take the fallback; steady decode builds take the view).
LLAMA_DISABLE_RS_STATE_VIEW=1 restores stock everywhere.

Measured (runner box, same-binary toggle, 28-patch base + 0029):

- decode trace: get_rows_float_vec (990 x 4.93us) and k_get_rows_float
  (990 x 1.65us) both eliminated; total decode kernel time 215.04 ->
  203.78ms per 33 tokens (-5.2%)
- tg128 toggle A/B, 5+3 interleaved rounds: 119.83-119.97 ->
  127.73-127.91 tok/s (+6.6%, 8/8 rounds separated)
- tg64@d16384: 111.63-111.77 -> 117.32-117.60 (+5.1% - the long board
  gains too); pp512 neutral (4149-4223 both arms)
- ppl (runner corpus, -c 512 --chunks 8, 3 loads): 3.9271/3.9301/3.9297
  vs stock 3.9314 (-0.03% to -0.11%, band 0.5%, verified-series cluster)
- server greedy vs 28-patch control bin dir: 5/6 prompts BYTE-EXACT
  (short/mid/code/math/summary); the 2k-token long prompt drifts at a
  77% common prefix on a near-tie token - the same request also flips
  on the CONTROL binary itself across repeated identical requests
  (measured: control in-process runs 1v2 and 2v3 both differ), i.e. the
  drift class predates this patch and is ppl-gated as in 0024/0026/0028.
- concurrent short-prompt server smoke (8 requests, 4 threads): coherent
  and correct; test-backend-ops MUL_MAT suite OK.
---
diff --git a/src/llama-graph.cpp b/src/llama-graph.cpp
index e12a8cdc2..dd50a0eb1 100644
--- a/src/llama-graph.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-graph.cpp
@@ -3287,7 +3287,8 @@ ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_rs(
            uint32_t   rs_head,
            uint32_t   rs_size,
             int32_t   rs_zero,
-        const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows) const {
+        const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows,
+              bool   state_is_identity) const {
 
     GGML_UNUSED(rs_size);
     ggml_tensor * states = ggml_reshape_2d(ctx0, s, state_size, s->ne[1]);
@@ -3300,7 +3301,19 @@ ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_rs(
     // copy states
     // NOTE: assuming the copy destinations are ALL contained between rs_head and rs_head + n_rs
     // {state_size, rs_size} -> {state_size, n_seqs}
-    ggml_tensor * output_states = get_state_rows(ctx0, states, state_copy_main);
+    // When every source row is the destination row itself (steady-state decode:
+    // no seq-copy migration, no rollback-snapshot restore - detected side-effect-
+    // free at graph build time), the gather is a pure materialization of rows
+    // [rs_head, rs_head + n_seqs) and is replaced by a contiguous view of the
+    // cache: byte-identical values reach the consumer and the per-layer state
+    // copy disappears. The view keeps the same execution-order reliance on the
+    // rs_zero clear that the get_rows form already has.
+    ggml_tensor * output_states;
+    if (state_is_identity) {
+        output_states = ggml_view_2d(ctx0, states, state_size, n_seqs, states->nb[1], rs_head*states->nb[1]);
+    } else {
+        output_states = get_state_rows(ctx0, states, state_copy_main);
+    }
     ggml_build_forward_expand(gf, output_states);
 
     // copy extra states which won't be changed further (between n_seqs and n_rs)
@@ -3348,12 +3361,25 @@ ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_rs(
         ggml_tensor * s,
             int32_t   state_size,
             int32_t   n_seqs,
-        const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows) const {
+        const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows,
+              bool   allow_state_view) const {
     const auto * kv_state = inp->mctx;
 
+    // Reuse safety: a built graph bakes the view offset while the fork reuses
+    // graphs across decode steps (only ~27 builds serve a 256-token completion
+    // here), so the view is additionally restricted to the single-slot serving
+    // shape (n_seqs == 1, head == 0, n_rs == 1). There the baked offset is row 0
+    // always - a reused view graph can never go stale - and this is exactly the
+    // ranked serving configuration (--parallel 1), so the full decode gain is
+    // kept. Multi-slot or migrated states fall back to the stock gather.
+    static const bool disable_state_view = getenv("LLAMA_DISABLE_RS_STATE_VIEW") != nullptr;
+    const bool state_is_identity = allow_state_view && !disable_state_view &&
+        n_seqs == 1 && kv_state->get_head() == 0 && kv_state->get_n_rs() == 1 &&
+        kv_state->s_copy_main_is_identity(n_seqs);
+
     return build_rs(s, inp->s_copy_main, inp->s_copy_extra, state_size, n_seqs,
                     kv_state->get_n_rs(), kv_state->get_head(), kv_state->get_size(), kv_state->get_rs_z(),
-                    get_state_rows);
+                    get_state_rows, state_is_identity);
 }
 
 ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_rwkv_token_shift_load(
